@dummdidumm @trueadm I found another issue with reactivity broken with `5.19.5` (works in `5.19.4`) and is not resolved as of `5.19.9` (the above issue was).  

The lockable tooltip [example](https://www.layerchart.com/docs/components/AreaChart#locking_and_clickable_tooltip) which uses `svelte:window` set a variable and pass it via `<Chart tooltip={{ locked }}>` stopped working in `5.19.5`.  I tried a few things to work around the issue (interestingly if I add some `console.log({ locked })` in TooltipContext it fixes it when Vite hot reloads, but refreshing the page breaks again.

I don't have much time to submit a proper issue, but will try to tonight.  Just wanted to mention it here as a comment in case it was related.

@trueadm I [documented](https://github.com/techniq/layerchart/issues/384) some LayerChart regressions I identified while running `5.19.5`.  Oddly, one is only visible when ran locally.  Due to the number of them, I'm going to downgrade the docs back to `5.19.4`, especially until I can dig into smaller reproductions.  Many are fairly complicated reactivity situations which will take a bit to boil down.

One quick observation is it seems the issue is possibly related to being nested within an object of a prop (for example)

```svelte
<Chart
  geo={{
    projection,
    fitGeojson: geojson,
    rotate: {
      yaw,
      pitch,
      roll,
    },
    scale,
  }}
>
```

```svelte
<AreaChart
  tooltip={{ locked: lockedTooltip }}
>
```

```svelte
<Chart
  brush={{
    mode: "separated",
    xDomain,
    onchange: (e) => (xDomain = e.xDomain),
    onreset: (e) => (xDomain = null),
  }}
>
```
